### Step 1 – Publish a report to Power BI Service

#### What I did in Power BI
- Logged into Power BI Desktop and Service with my org account  
  (`...@TerhaarAnalytics.onmicrosoft.com`).
- Opened my Project 2 report PBIX.
- Clicked **Home → Publish** and selected **My workspace**.
- In Power BI Service (app.powerbi.com), verified that:
  - A **Report** appeared with the PBIX name.
  - A **Semantic model (dataset)** appeared with the same name.
- Opened the report in the Service and tested slicers/filters.
- Changed a visual title in Desktop and published again.
- Confirmed that the report in the Service updated after republish.

#### What I learned
- Power BI Service is the cloud environment for hosting reports,
  dashboards, workspaces and semantic models.
- Publishing from Desktop sends **two artefacts**:
  - the **report** (visuals + layout),
  - the **semantic model/dataset** (data model + queries).
- A publish with the same name **overwrites** the existing report and
  updates the dataset in that workspace.
- Desktop = build & model; Service = share, manage, secure, and monitor.
- I must be logged in with my **org account** in both Desktop & Service
  to publish successfully.

